# Video engine

This repo's **production videos** are the `channel/` documentary engine, not `graph/` `ideate`. A title naming a real person belongs on `python -m channel generate`, never the LangGraph topic flow.

Canonical command: `python -m channel generate --channel <mode> --title "<title>"`. Drop-folder cut: `python -m channel drop --channel <mode> --title "<title>"` then assemble. Jobs live in `artifacts/<JOB_ID>/`. Specs: `docs/video-engine/`. Operator loop is the **master prompt** (`channel/master_prompt.py` / `MASTER`): same stages on every channel, DNA customized per mode. Quiet Wealth uses the v13 celebrity and life POV master in `channel/wealth_prompts.py`. Copy the grammar in `docs/video-engine/QUALITY_BAR.md`; never clone a reference-cut spine. Quiet Wealth still grammar is in `docs/wealth-pov.md`.

```text
DO NOT MODIFY THE VIDEO ENGINE, CHANNEL PROMPTS, GLOBAL STYLE, MODEL CONFIGURATION, OR QA THRESHOLDS DURING A NORMAL VIDEO GENERATION TASK.
```

Images: `python -m channel images` (Nano Banana 2 / `gemini-3.1-flash-image`) when `GEMINI_API_KEY` is set, after `originality_score ≥ 80` and `ready_to_publish`; or operator **Google Flow** stills from `flow_prompts.txt`; or drop-folder stills named `[00-00]_….jpg`. Optional motion: `python -m channel videos` (`gemini-omni-1.1-flash` image-to-video) after stills exist; assemble prefers `videos/{still-stem}.mp4` and otherwise holds the still. Voice: Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS (`python -m channel tts`, `gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview`) when `GEMINI_API_KEY` is set; otherwise **imported audio** (`ingest-audio` or a file in `drop/`). Engine never calls ElevenLabs or Flow. Shipped recuts may still use Kokoro (`am_liam` / roster). No silent provider fallback. Drop-folder cuts assemble without burned captions.

After a production change, update `docs/custom-videos.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `.cursor/rules/custom-videos.mdc` together. `tests/test_channel_handoff.py` guards the surfaces.
